<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- What lets `UNNotificationContent.updating(from:)` render a banner as a
	     COMMUNICATION notification — the sender's face where the app icon
	     normally sits, rather than a thumbnail beside it.

	     REQUIRES "Communication Notifications" enabled on THIS extension's own
	     App ID (com.walhallaa.chatTest-20241220.NotificationService) as well as
	     the app's, and it fails the build loudly if it is missing, the way
	     time-sensitive does next door in Runner.entitlements.

	     Worth knowing because the tooling says otherwise: Xcode's portal
	     database lists this capability as supported on an application and a
	     watchkit2-extension and NOT on an ordinary app extension. That list is
	     wrong — the portal offers the checkbox anyway, and both binaries here
	     ship signed with the entitlement. It is wrong about App Groups on the
	     Share Extension in exactly the same way. Do not use it to conclude a
	     capability is unavailable. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.usernotifications.communication</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- The App Group this extension parks an arriving message in, so the app
	     can open the room already showing it instead of asking the network for
	     something the phone has just been told. ShareGroup.swift owns the
	     identifier and the container lookup; this extension is its third
	     member, after Runner and the Share Extension.

	     SAME provisioning caveat as everywhere else this appears: App Groups
	     must be enabled on THIS extension's own App ID
	     (com.walhallaa.chatTest-20241220.NotificationService) in the portal, not
	     only on the app's. Get it wrong and nothing fails loudly — it builds, it
	     signs, it runs, and `containerURL` simply returns nil forever. That is
	     what the NSLog in `stage(_:)` is for. And per the note above, Xcode's
	     portal database is wrong about App Groups on an app extension in
	     exactly the same way it is wrong about communication notifications;
	     the checkbox is offered and works. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.walhallaa.monkeyhub</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
